    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll** (74.50) and **Brice Turang** (73.40), our two premier threats for stolen base production. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Woodruff, where his elite sprint speed is amplified by the pitcher's slower delivery, effectively weaponizing his ability to swipe bags. Similarly, **Brice Turang** draws a favorable pairing against Meibrys Viloria; provided he hits in the projected #3 hole, his combination of SP skill-differential and order position makes him a high-efficiency engine for our Roto categories. **Josh Naylor** (71.12) and **Mickey Moniak** (69.72) round out our top-tier targets, with **Mickey Moniak** specifically gaining significant value from a park factor boost (+14%) despite the L/L disadvantage against Robbie Ray.\n\nOur most difficult roster management decision centered on the utility spot, where **Kyle Karros** (63.93) edged out **Cole Young** (50.21). While **Cole Young** possesses high-end potential, his overall projected efficiency against Shane Bieber didn't eclipse the park-adjusted output we expect from **Kyle Karros** in his current matchup. We are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key players, including **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, both of whom see their scores fluctuate significantly based on their final batting order. **James Wood** (52.66) remains a high-risk, high-reward play; his elite xwOBA (0.418) is being suppressed by an elite defensive catcher, but his #1 spot in the lineup keeps his floor viable. Note that **Tyler Soderstrom** remains on the IL, while bench stashes like **Isaac Paredes**, **Travis Bazzana**, and the rest of our depth\u2014including **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, and **Edwin Arroyo**\u2014stand ready should late-breaking injury news or lineup adjustments necessitate a pivot.",
